From 734cea265257f8029e2e1f9724e3f6bd0368bfa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 20:41:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04340/11362] [outer-loop] Fix .446 A1 brace-templating: escape
 literal {lp85,r11l,tu93}/{game:...}

The conductor's DOGFOOD pre-flight caught a brace error in the .446 A1 prompt
(exp4841-a1: KeyError 'game') -- single-brace literals like {lp85, r11l, tu93}
and {game: {...}} collide with the conductor's str.format() templating
({date}/{project_root}). The auto-fix is in-process only; the persisted file
still carried the fragile bug. Rephrased all such literals to brace-free prose
("the three games (lp85, r11l, tu93)") so .format() renders cleanly without
relying on the auto-fixer. Verified: all string fields across all 10 tasks now
pass .format(date=...,project_root=...). Level-up/overdue/url lints clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
